id=a52sxq_launch_tuning
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: faster app resume (lz4 zram, vendor upmigrate)
author=kusti420
description=Measured on 9.3.36 (agent profiling, 2026-10-15): the slow part of using apps is resuming one that sat idle, whose memory is in zram (8 GB with RAM Plus) and partly in the RAM Plus backing file: Samsung Internet's resume read 7,675 pages back from swap (864 ms). zram now compresses with lz4 instead of lzo-rle (much faster to decompress on the A78/A55 cores, slightly lower ratio). The Qualcomm perf HAL (perf-hal-2-2) records sched_upmigrate when it starts, before the vendor post_boot script has set 71 95, so it recorded the kernel default 94 94 and put that back after every launch boost (temporary test with 71 95 kept: launcher janky frames 5.9% -> 3.3-4.6%). Once the vendor script is done (vendor.post_boot.parsed=1, after sys.boot_completed) the rc writes the vendor's sched_downmigrate 65 85 and sched_upmigrate 71 95 again and restarts the perf HAL, which then records 71 95. RAM Plus itself stays a user setting (Device care > Memory).
